Subject: [PATCH] plat: stm32mp2: force dual-core on STM32MP257F-DK

stm32mp_is_single_core() misreads the OTP part number on the USB serial-boot
(DFU) path and reports the dual-core MP257 as single-core, so PSCI refuses to
start CPU1 (kernel: 'psci: failed to boot CPU1 (-95)'), breaking the power-
domain tree. Force the MP251 single-core case to false for this board.

--- a/plat/st/stm32mp2/stm32mp2_private.c	2026-06-05 06:09:41.414106105 -0700
+++ b/plat/st/stm32mp2/stm32mp2_private.c	2026-06-05 06:09:41.418106134 -0700
@@ -518,7 +518,7 @@
 	case STM32MP251D_PART_NB:
 	case STM32MP251F_PART_NB:
 #endif /* STM32MP25 */
-		single_core = true;
+		single_core = false; /* STM32MP257F-DK is dual-core: OTP part-number read is unreliable on USB serial-boot and can misdetect single-core, blocking CPU1 */
 		break;
 	default:
 		break;
